Wrong (A): Redemptions treated as distributions under Section 301 do reduce E&P; they are not ignored simply because stock is involved.
Wrong (B): E&P is not increased by a redemption. The corporation pays cash out, reducing its economic capacity to distribute, not increasing it.
Wrong (D): The pro rata E&P reduction rule under Section 312(n)(7) applies only when the redemption qualifies as an exchange under Section 302(b), which it does not here.$EXPL$
