  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 316, earnings and profits measure a corporation''s economic ability to distribute dividends. E&P determines whether distributions to shareholders are taxed as dividends, return of capital, or capital gain under the Section 301 ordering rules.
Wrong (B): Taxable income is computed independently on Form 1120. E&P is a separate concept that starts with taxable income but includes additional adjustments not reflected on the return.
Wrong (C): The dividends received deduction under Section 243 applies to dividends a corporation receives from other corporations, not to measuring its own distribution capacity.
