-- Q11086: C Corporations [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 269, if any person acquires control of a corporation and the principal purpose is to evade or avoid federal income tax by securing a deduction not otherwise available, the IRS may disallow the deduction entirely. Unlike Section 382, which merely limits annual NOL usage, Section 269 provides complete disallowance.
Wrong (A): Section 382 imposes only a rate limitation on NOL usage after an ownership change. It is not the IRS''s only tool when tax avoidance is the principal purpose.
Wrong (C): The step transaction doctrine recharacterizes multi-step transactions but does not independently eliminate NOL carryforwards.
Wrong (D): Section 482 governs transfer pricing allocations between related parties and does not address NOL deduction disallowance.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11086;

