-- Q11090: C Corporations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 357(c), when liabilities assumed ($100,000) exceed the total adjusted basis of property transferred ($75,000) in a Section 351 exchange, the excess ($25,000) is recognized as gain. The stock basis is computed as $75,000 minus $100,000 plus $25,000 gain recognized, equaling $0.
Wrong (A): Section 357(c) triggers gain recognition regardless of the property''s FMV when liabilities exceed basis. A $0 gain and $75,000 basis ignores the liability-over-basis rule.
Wrong (B): $175,000 represents the full difference between FMV and basis, but Section 351 limits recognized gain to the excess of liabilities over basis, not the full realized gain.
Wrong (D): $100,000 gain equal to the full mortgage is incorrect because only the excess of liabilities over basis ($25,000) triggers recognition, and a $150,000 basis has no support under Section 358.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11090;

