  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 547, a corporation may claim a deduction for deficiency dividends paid within 90 days of a PHC tax determination, which eliminates the PHC tax liability. However, Sterling must still pay applicable interest and penalties on the underlying tax deficiency from the original due date.
Wrong (A): While the deficiency dividend eliminates the PHC tax itself, interest and penalties on the late determination are still owed and cannot be avoided.
