-- Q11099: C Corporations [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 312(k), E&P must use the alternative depreciation system (ADS), which requires straight-line depreciation over longer recovery periods and does not allow bonus depreciation. Since tax depreciation (bonus + MACRS) exceeds ADS depreciation, taxable income is lower than E&P, making E&P higher.
Wrong (A): E&P uses ADS straight-line depreciation, which is slower than MACRS, so E&P will be higher than taxable income, not lower.
Wrong (B): Section 312(k)(3)(A) specifically disallows bonus depreciation for E&P computation purposes, so E&P and taxable income will not be equal.
Wrong (C): E&P does allow depreciation deductions, but they must be computed using ADS straight-line rather than accelerated methods or bonus depreciation.$EXPL$
