  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 755, the Section 743(b) adjustment is allocated between ordinary income assets and capital gain assets based on the difference between the transferee''s share of FMV and inside basis within each class. Shaw''s ordinary share is $150,000 FMV vs. $75,000 basis ($75,000 adjustment); capital share is $200,000 FMV vs. $25,000 basis ($175,000 adjustment).
Wrong (A): $50,000 to ordinary assets understates the allocation because it does not correctly compute Shaw''s 25% share of the FMV-to-basis difference for ordinary income property.
Wrong (B): An equal $125,000 split ignores Section 755''s requirement to allocate based on the FMV-to-basis difference within each asset class separately.
