  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 708(b)(1), a partnership terminates only when no part of its business, financial operation, or venture continues to be carried on by any of its partners in a partnership. This is the sole remaining termination trigger after the TCJA repealed the technical termination rule.
Wrong (A): The TCJA of 2017 repealed the technical termination rule that previously applied when 50% or more of interests were sold within 12 months.
Wrong (C): Admission of a new partner, regardless of capital contribution size, does not trigger termination under current Section 708(b)(1).
