-- Q11102: Partnerships [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1223(2), when property is transferred to a partnership under Section 721 with a carryover basis, the partnership tacks the contributing partner''s holding period. Because Ellison held the land for 8 years, the partnership''s holding period exceeds 8 years, qualifying any gain for long-term capital gain treatment.
Wrong (A): The holding period does not restart at the contribution date. A fresh holding period would apply only if the partnership received a FMV basis rather than a carryover basis.
Wrong (C): There is no 12-month default measured from the start of the partnership''s tax year for contributed property holding periods.
Wrong (D): Six months is not a default holding period for partnership contributed assets under any provision of the IRC.$EXPL$
