-- Q11106: Partnerships [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 752 and Treas. Reg. Section 1.752-2, a partner''s loan to the partnership creates a recourse liability allocated to the partner bearing the economic risk of loss. Because only Garrett bears repayment risk, the entire $80,000 is allocated to Garrett''s basis. Hansen has no repayment obligation and receives no basis increase.
Wrong (A): Splitting the liability $40,000 each based on profit-sharing ratios applies only to nonrecourse liabilities under Treas. Reg. Section 1.752-3, not recourse liabilities.
Wrong (C): Both partners'' bases increasing by $80,000 each would double-count the liability, which totals only $80,000.
Wrong (D): Partner loans create partnership liabilities that increase outside basis under Section 752, even though they are not capital contributions.$EXPL$
