-- Q11112: Partnerships [hard/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Treas. Reg. Section 1.752-2(b), recourse liabilities are allocated to the partner who bears the economic risk of loss. In a constructive liquidation, Monroe has an unlimited deficit restoration obligation and must restore any deficit, bearing the entire $500,000 risk. Nash, as a limited partner with no DRO, bears no economic risk beyond her capital.
Wrong (A): Profit-sharing ratios apply to nonrecourse liability allocations under Treas. Reg. Section 1.752-3, not to recourse liabilities where economic risk of loss controls.
Wrong (C): An equal $250,000 split ignores the economic risk of loss analysis, which allocates based on who must restore deficits, not equally.
Wrong (D): Capital contribution ratios are not the basis for recourse liability allocation; the constructive liquidation analysis under Reg. Section 1.752-2(b) governs.$EXPL$
