-- Q11113: Partnerships [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 761(c), any modification to the partnership agreement made before the filing deadline (including extensions) is treated as if made during the applicable tax year. However, the special allocation of depreciation must independently satisfy the substantial economic effect test under Section 704(b) and Treas. Reg. Section 1.704-1(b)(2).
Wrong (A): Post-year amendments are not per se invalid. Section 761(c) specifically permits retroactive modifications made before the filing deadline.
Wrong (C): While the timing is valid under Section 761(c), the special allocation is not automatically respected; it must meet the Section 704(b) substantial economic effect requirements.
Wrong (D): Section 761(c) does not require IRS permission for retroactive effect. The amendment is valid if made before the return filing deadline.$EXPL$
