-- Q11114: Partnerships [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 731(a)(2), a loss is recognized to a partner only in a liquidating distribution and only when the distribution consists solely of money, unrealized receivables, and inventory with a value less than the partner''s outside basis. No loss is recognized in current distributions.
Wrong (B): Loss recognition is not based on FMV comparisons in any distribution. Section 731(a)(2) requires liquidating treatment and a restricted asset composition.
Wrong (C): Current (nonliquidating) distributions never produce a recognized loss regardless of the basis reduction, only liquidating distributions qualify.
Wrong (D): The comparison of distributed property''s FMV to its inside basis is not the test for partner loss recognition under Section 731.$EXPL$
