-- Q11115: Partnerships [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 724(a), any unrealized receivable contributed by a partner retains its ordinary income character in the partnership''s hands. When collected or disposed of, the gain or income is ordinary regardless of the partnership''s accounting method, preventing conversion to capital gain through contribution.
Wrong (B): Conversion to capital gain property is the exact mischaracterization Section 724 was designed to prevent. The receivable does not change character upon contribution.
Wrong (C): Section 1231 treatment applies to depreciable business property held more than one year, not to unrealized receivables contributed under Section 721.
Wrong (D): The partnership''s accounting method is irrelevant to the character determination. Section 724(a) mandates ordinary income treatment regardless of method.$EXPL$
